# Git commit policy

## Message body

Commit message **bodies** must not contain:

- Email addresses (`name@domain`)
- `Co-authored-by` or any line containing the word **author**
- AI/agent attribution trailers (Cursor, Claude, Codex, etc.)

Write only a short technical description in the body.

## Hooks (do not bypass)

`.githooks/prepare-commit-msg` strips agent-injected trailers. `commit-msg` rejects violations. `pre-push` blocks pushes with bad messages.

**Never run `git commit --no-verify` or `git push --no-verify`.** Agents often use `--no-verify` to skip slow `pre-commit` checks; that also skips message policy hooks and is how `Co-authored-by: … <contact@example.com>` trailers reach the remote.

If `pre-commit` is too slow, fix or scope the change — do not skip hooks for commits.

## Identity

Use the human dev identity (`GIT_USERNAME` / `GIT_EMAIL` on Cloud Agent). Do not commit as Cursor, Claude, GitLab project-bot, or similar.
